wmctrl: Crucial for managing windows in the DE (e.g., positioning, resizing, or controlling windows programmatically in your brick architecture).
nmap, net-tools, tcpdump: Useful for network-related features (e.g., scanning for devices, debugging connections).
lsof, iotop, htop: Help monitor system resources while developing, ensuring the DE isn’t overloading the system.
smartmontools, lsblk, fdisk, parted: Support disk and hardware management features (e.g., detecting drives, managing partitions).
libmtp, gphoto2, usbutils: Enable device detection (phones, cameras) for potential DE integrations.
rsync, testdisk, photorec, john: Provide recovery and utility functions for robustness.